    <name>
      <text>Sum arithmatic q2</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The learners of a Junior School start a Savings Club. In week 1, the club saves Ksh {@t1@}. In week 2, it saves Ksh {@t2@}. In week 3, it saves Ksh {@t3@}. Each week, the club saves the same amount more than in the week before.</p>

<p>(a) Find the common difference, \(d\).</p>
<p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>

<p>(b) How much does the club save in week {@p@}?</p>
<p>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>

<p>(c) Use the formula to find the total amount the club saves in the first {@q@} weeks.</p>
<p>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The weekly savings are {@t1@}, {@t2@}, {@t3@}, {@t4@}, ... This is an arithmetic progression (AP), because the same amount is added each week.</p>

<p>(a) <strong>Common difference:</strong></p>
<p>Take any term and subtract the term before it:</p>
<p>\[ d = {@t2@} - {@t1@} = {@ta1@} \]</p>
<p>Check: \( {@t3@} - {@t2@} = {@ta1@} \). The difference is always the same, so the club saves Ksh {@ta1@} more each week.</p>

<p>(b) <strong>Savings in week {@p@}:</strong></p>
<p>The rule for the \(n^{th}\) term of an AP is:</p>
<p>\[ T_n = a + (n-1)d \]</p>
<p>Here \( a = {@a@} \), \( d = {@d@} \) and \( n = {@p@} \). Put these into the rule:</p>
<p>\[ T_{ {@p@} } = {@a@} + ({@p@} - 1) \times {@d@} \]</p>
<p>\[ T_{ {@p@} } = {@a@} + {@(p-1)*d@} = {@ta2@} \]</p>
<p>In week {@p@}, the club saves Ksh {@ta2@}.</p>

<p>(c) <strong>Total savings in the first {@q@} weeks:</strong></p>
<p>The sum of the first \(n\) terms of an AP is:</p>
<p>\[ S_n = \frac{n}{2}\left(2a + (n-1)d\right) \]</p>
<p>Now \( n = {@q@} \). The values of \(a\) and \(d\) stay the same. Put the values into the formula:</p>
<p>\[ S_{ {@q@} } = \frac{ {@q@} }{2}\left(2 \times {@a@} + ({@q@} - 1) \times {@d@}\right) \]</p>
<p>Work out the bracket:</p>
<p>\[ S_{ {@q@} } = \frac{ {@q@} }{2}\left({@2*a@} + {@(q-1)*d@}\right) = \frac{ {@q@} }{2} \times {@2*a + (q-1)*d@} \]</p>
<p>Multiply:</p>
<p>\[ S_{ {@q@} } = {@ta3@} \]</p>
<p>The club saves a total of Ksh {@ta3@} in the first {@q@} weeks.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
